<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Entitlements for the signed Miolingo.app.

    App Sandbox is deliberately OFF (the app shells out to /opt/local/bin/espeak
    and reads a SQLite DB outside a container). With the sandbox off, the
    com.apple.security.* sandbox keys do nothing, so we do NOT set
    com.apple.security.app-sandbox.

    The microphone and speech-recognition prompts are driven by the
    Info.plist usage strings + the TCC subsystem, which key off a STABLE code
    signature. Signing (even ad-hoc) is what lets the Speech Recognition
    prompt appear and the grant persist; these entitlements document intent
    and are required if App Sandbox is ever enabled later.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.microphone</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
